## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates knowledge of practical data-structure trade-offs for dynamic ranking. Candidates should justify when to sort on demand vs. maintain auxiliary structures.

## Key Concepts
- Hash map for O(1) key access
- On-demand sorting for top-k retrieval
- Trade-off: simpler updates vs. slower top-k retrieval

## Code Example
```javascript
class CounterTopK {
  constructor() {
    this.counts = new Map(); // key -> count
  }
  add(key, delta) {
    const cur = this.counts.get(key) || 0;
    const next = cur + delta;
    if (next <= 0) this.counts.delete(key); else this.counts.set(key, next);
  }
  get(key) { return this.counts.get(key) || 0; }
  topK(k) {
    const arr = Array.from(this.counts.entries());
    arr.sort((a,b)=> b[1]-a[1] || a[0].localeCompare(b[0]));
    return arr.slice(0,k).map(([key]) => key);
  }
}
```

